      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-01-05T05:34:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These two bullets read a bit contradicting. Is it that we first pick a matching route per routing table / agent, preferring one with a lower weight, then we do per-agent round-robin?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "efe9d6acef98f5d6f9cebc527d118f9343937904",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa81d914_65866bbb",
        "filename": "docs/operation-guide/src/routing/section_routing_overview_ja.adoc",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002753
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-01-19T02:28:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The second bullet point only applies when there are multiple matching routes.\n\nIn English it reads as follows:\n\n* Attempts to match a given packet’s destination with a route in its routing table based on the packet’s source and destination, preferring the route with the lower weight value.\n\n* For packets with more than one matching route, uses per-agent round robin selection among those routes.",
      "parentUuid": "fa81d914_9be8517e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "efe9d6acef98f5d6f9cebc527d118f9343937904",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735",
      "unresolved": false
    },
